Master Prompt: Rajasthani D2C + B2B E-Commerce Website
Research-backed, copy-paste prompt for an AI builder (Claude Code, Cursor, Lovable, v0, etc.)
Part 1: Research Summary (what the prompt is built on)
Brands studied: Fabindia, Anokhi, Jaipur Rugs, Jaypore, iTokri, Okhai, Good Earth.
What they do well (and the prompt copies):
• Artisan provenance. Anokhi sources from artisan cooperatives around Jaipur and sells on documented craft origin. Jaipur Rugs grew from two looms and nine weavers to over 7,000 looms and 40,000 artisans, and tells that story everywhere. So every product page needs a maker story, a craft origin and a GI/authenticity badge.
• Price transparency and trust. Rajasthani handicraft pricing is often opaque, with markups of several times cost. A transparent 'Where your money goes' breakdown is a real differentiator.
• Content-led commerce. iTokri and Anokhi run craft blogs and museum-style storytelling (for example the Anokhi Museum of Hand Printing). Education sells handmade goods.
• Personalisation. Jaipur Rugs' D2C review (MICA study) stresses personalised touchpoints across the customer lifecycle. D2C's edge over marketplaces is personalisation and fast feedback loops.
• Omnichannel and B2B. Established players run D2C alongside wholesale, export and corporate gifting, and explain how D2C complements retail partners rather than competing with them.
Rajasthani visual and craft vocabulary (the design system draws from this):
• Textiles: Sanganeri block print (fine florals on white or off-white), Bagru and Dabu (earthy indigo, red, black, geometric, natural dyes), Bandhani (tie-dye dots), Leheriya (diagonal wave stripes, once a Rajput turban marker), Kota Doria, Jaipuri razai quilts, dhurries. Block printing uses gadh (background), rekh (outline) and datta (fill) blocks.
• Jewellery: Meenakari (enamel), Kundan and Jadau, Thewa (gold fused on glass, Pratapgarh, GI tag 2014), lac bangles, tribal silver.
• Art: Phad scroll paintings (Shahpura, ~700 years old), Pichwai, miniature painting, Kathputli puppets, Blue Pottery (Jaipur).
• Architecture: Jharokha windows, Hawa Mahal lattice (jaali), cusped arches, chhatris, havelis, stepwells, Mehrangarh and Amer forts, Pink City.
• Colour: turmeric yellow, kesariya saffron, Jaipur pink, marigold orange, indigo (Bagru), peacock green, maroon and sindoor red, desert sand, gold zari.
• Culture and sound: Ghoomar dance, Manganiyar music, camel caravans, Pushkar fair, Teej, Gangaur, Holi, Diwali, kulhad chai.
Part 2: The Prompt (copy everything below this line)
ROLE
You are a senior full-stack engineer, UX designer and motion designer. Build a production-ready, end-to-end D2C + B2B e-commerce website for a premium Rajasthani handcrafted brand. Deliver working code, not mockups. Work in phases, run and test each phase, and explain assumptions briefly.
1. BRAND
• Working name: Rangrez Haveli (replace with [BRAND_NAME]).
• Tagline: 'Rajasthan, crafted by hand. Delivered to your door.'
• Positioning: Premium but accessible, artisan-first, ethically made, with documented craft provenance (the Anokhi, Fabindia and Jaipur Rugs playbook, in a more joyful and modern wrapper).
• Voice: Warm, proud, playful. Light Hinglish touches in microcopy ('Padharo!' to welcome, 'Mhare Rajasthan' in the footer, 'Chai pe charcha' for the blog) with full English clarity. Always provide an EN / हिन्दी toggle.
• Audiences: (a) D2C shoppers in India and the diaspora, gift buyers; (b) B2B buyers: retailers, interior designers, hotels and resorts, corporate gifting, export importers.
2. TECH STACK (use unless I say otherwise)
• Frontend: Next.js 14+ (App Router, TypeScript), Tailwind CSS, shadcn/ui primitives, Framer Motion plus GSAP (ScrollTrigger) and Lenis smooth scroll, Lottie for micro-illustrations, optional React Three Fiber only for one hero effect.
• State and data: Zustand (cart, wishlist, UI), TanStack Query, Zod validation.
• Backend: Next.js route handlers or tRPC, PostgreSQL with Prisma, Redis (cache, rate limit), NextAuth/Auth.js (email OTP, Google, phone OTP).
• Payments (India-first): Razorpay (UPI, cards, netbanking, wallets, EMI) plus Cash on Delivery with a small verification step; Stripe/PayPal for international orders.
• Other services: Meilisearch or Algolia (search), Cloudinary (images, video, AVIF/WebP), Sanity or MDX (blog CMS), Resend (transactional email), WhatsApp Business API links (order updates, support), Shiprocket/Delhivery (shipping, pincode check), GST-compliant invoice PDF generation.
• Quality: Lighthouse 90+ on mobile, WCAG 2.2 AA, SEO (SSR/ISR, JSON-LD, sitemap), i18n-ready, Playwright e2e tests for the checkout and B2B flows.
• Seed the database with realistic data at the very end of development (see sections 7 and 13).
3. DESIGN SYSTEM: 'Modern Rajputana'
Palette (CSS variables, WCAG-checked):
• Day mode 'Dhoop': background sand-ivory #FBF3E4, surface #FFFFFF, ink deep-maroon-brown #2A1410, primary Jaipur pink-maroon #B3123F, accent kesariya #F28C1B, secondary turmeric #F4B400, indigo #1F3A93, peacock green #0F7B6C, gold #C9A227.
• Night mode 'Raat': background midnight indigo #0E1226, surface #171C3A, ink #F6EBD6, same accents slightly lifted; gold zari glows; subtle star-field and lantern effects.
• Optional third mode 'Tyohaar' (festive): confetti, extra gold, marigold garlands on cards, auto-suggested near Diwali, Holi and Teej.
• Mode toggle is a sun/moon charkha-style switch with a smooth radial-wipe transition. Respect system preference and remember the choice.
Typography: Display: a high-contrast serif with character (Playfair Display, Cormorant, or Yatra One for hero words). Body: Inter or Poppins. Devanagari: Tiro Devanagari Hindi or Noto Sans Devanagari. Section numbers in a 'Rozha One' style for a poster feel.
Rajasthani UI elements (build as reusable SVG/CSS components):
• Jharokha arch frames for hero media, modals and product images (cusped arch clip-path).
• Jaali lattice patterns as section dividers and subtle background textures (Hawa Mahal).
• Bandhani dot grid as loaders, bullet points and hover patterns.
• Block-print border strips (Sanganeri floral, Bagru geometric) as animated section borders that 'stamp' in on scroll.
• Leheriya wave stripes as button hover fills and page transitions.
• Meenakari-style badges for 'Handmade', 'GI Tagged', 'Bestseller'.
• Phad-scroll storytelling: horizontally scrolling painted-scroll panels on the About page.
• Kathputli puppet mascot (small, strings animated) that appears on empty states, 404 and cart-empty pages.
• Chhatri and fort silhouettes as parallax layers; marigold garland drape across the header on festive mode.
• Rounded 'haveli window' cards, gold hairline borders, paper-grain texture overlay at 3-4% opacity.
• Custom cursor: small gold lotus or turban-knot that scales on hover (desktop only).
• Sound: optional, off by default. A 'mute/unmute' toggle for a soft sitar/rawanhatha loop and a tiny 'jhankar' on add to cart.
4. THE LOADER (make it crazy and joyful)
Build a 'Baraat Loader' that plays on first visit per session and when heavy pages load. Max about 2.8 s total, skippable ('Skip, mujhe jaldi hai'), and never blocks content longer than needed (progress is tied to real asset loading, with a minimum of about 1.6 s so the animation lands).
Sequence:
1.  Night-indigo screen. A single diya flickers; its flame draws a jharokha arch outline.
2.  A bandhani dot mandala assembles dot by dot in the arch; the dots fill with colour as the percentage counter (in Devanagari numerals that morph to English) climbs.
3.  A kathputli puppet drops in on strings, dances a ghoomar-style spin, tips its turban, then 'pulls' the arch open like curtains.
4.  A tiny camel caravan crosses the progress line at the bottom; the lead camel carries the % badge.
5.  Rotating humorous micro-messages, one every 700 ms: 'Chai ubal rahi hai…', 'Camel ko parking mil rahi hai', 'Block pe rang chadh raha hai', 'Haveli ke darwaze khul rahe hain…', 'Ghoomar ki taiyari chal rahi hai'.
6.  Exit: a colour-burst (Holi gulal / pichkari splash) radiates from the center; the arch zooms toward the viewer and its opening becomes the hero (shared-element handoff so there is no cut).
Rules: use Lottie/SVG plus GSAP, with no heavy video. Honour prefers-reduced-motion with a simple fade and logo. Cache so repeat visits within the session skip it. Also build smaller loaders: bandhani-dot spinner for buttons, leheriya shimmer skeletons for product grids, and a loom thread-weaving progress bar for route changes.
5. LANDING PAGE (must hook within 3 seconds)
Goal: a first screen that makes someone stop scrolling, then guides them to shop, with proven D2C conversion structure.
Sections, in order:
1.  Announcement bar: rotating offers ('Free shipping above ₹1,999', 'COD available', 'Wholesale? Get 40% margin: Join B2B') plus a language and mode toggle.
2.  Sticky header: logo, mega-menu (categories with image previews), search with instant suggestions and trending crafts, wishlist heart with count, account, cart drawer trigger, and a distinct 'B2B / Wholesale' pill.
3.  Hero: 'The Living Jharokha'. A full-viewport, jharokha-shaped window. Inside it, layered parallax (dunes, fort, sun, chhatri, birds) that reacts to cursor and mobile gyroscope. A headline reveals word by word ('Wear the desert. Gift a palace.'). Three CTAs: Shop Now, Explore Crafts, Shop Wholesale. A looping muted video of artisans (block printing, lac bangle making) plays in a small arch with 'Meet the maker' caption.
4.  Interactive banner carousel (5 slides), each a different interaction, auto-advance with progress ring and swipe/keyboard support:
    ◦ Block Print Studio: drag a slider to reveal a plain fabric becoming printed; click a block-stamp to 'print' a motif live.
    ◦ Bandhani Colour Switcher: choose swatches (kesariya, peacock, rani pink, indigo) and the product image recolours smoothly.
    ◦ Shop the Look: a styled haveli-room photo with clickable hotspots that pop product cards.
    ◦ Meenakari Spotlight: cursor-following light that makes enamel sparkle; 3D-tilt card.
    ◦ Festive Countdown: timer to the next festival (Diwali, Teej, Holi) with a gift-hamper CTA and confetti on hover.
5.  Trust strip: GI/authentic craft, free returns window, secure payments (UPI icons), artisan-made, pan-India and worldwide shipping, WhatsApp support.
6.  Shop by Category: 6 big arch-framed tiles with hover video previews.
7.  Bestsellers and New Arrivals: tabs plus horizontal snap-scroll with quick-add, wishlist heart (animated burst), and 'x people viewing' or low-stock urgency (honest data only).
8.  'Meet the Makers' scroll story: pinned section where Phad-style panels scroll horizontally, each showing an artisan, village, craft and the products they made.
9.  Craft Explorer: an interactive stylised Rajasthan map; click Sanganer, Bagru, Pratapgarh, Shahpura, Jodhpur, Bikaner, Jaipur to see the craft and shop it.
10.  Where your money goes: animated price-breakdown donut (artisan share, materials, logistics, brand), the transparency angle.
11.  B2B teaser band: 'Retailers, designers, hotels: wholesale pricing, custom designs, white-label.' With MOQ and margin calculator preview and a Request Catalogue button.
12.  Reviews and UGC: star ratings, photo reviews, Instagram-style grid, 'Wear it your way' gallery.
13.  Blog highlights, newsletter signup (first-order discount reward, spin-the-'Ghoomar chakra' wheel that opens after 20 s or on exit intent, once only), footer (links, policies, payment icons, social, address, FAQ, 'Mhare Rajasthan' sign-off with a tiny dancing kathputli).
Page-transition effect: leheriya diagonal wave wipe between routes. Scroll effects: block-print borders stamping in, jaali pattern parallax, reveal-on-scroll, counters, magnetic buttons, image zoom-on-hover, shared-element transitions from product card to product page.
6. CORE FEATURES (D2C)
Catalogue: 6 categories (see section 7) with sub-categories, filters (price, craft type, region, colour, size, material, occasion, rating, in-stock), sort, grid and list toggle, infinite scroll or pagination, active-filter chips, saved filters, recently viewed, 'Similar crafts' and 'Complete the look' recommendations.
Product page: zoomable gallery with 360/video, size and colour variants, stock and pincode delivery estimate, price with MRP and discount, craft passport (technique, region, GI tag, artisan name and photo, hours of work, care instructions), 'Where your money goes' mini-chart, customer Q&A, reviews with photos, size guide drawer, share, gift-wrap and message option, sticky add-to-cart on mobile, bundle upsell ('Buy the set and save'), back-in-stock alerts, Notify-me.
Wishlist ('Pasand'): heart on every card with animated burst, guest wishlist stored locally and merged on login, shareable wishlist link, move-to-cart, price-drop alerts.
Cart: slide-in drawer plus full page; quantity edit, save for later, coupon field, free-shipping progress bar ('Add ₹340 for free delivery'), gift options, cross-sell, estimated tax and delivery, abandoned-cart email/WhatsApp flow.
Checkout: guest or logged-in; 3 steps with progress (Address, Delivery, Payment); pincode auto-fill and serviceability check; saved addresses; UPI intent/QR, cards, netbanking, wallets, EMI, COD (OTP-confirmed), international cards; GST invoice details toggle; order summary; trust badges; error recovery; confetti and success page with order timeline and 'Share your haul' prompt.
Orders and account: order history, tracking timeline with courier status, invoice download, returns and exchanges with reason and pickup request, reorder, saved addresses and payment methods, profile with avatar, loyalty points ('Mohar' coins: earn on purchases, reviews, referrals; redeem at checkout), referral link, notification preferences, language, delete account.
Search: typo-tolerant, Hindi and English, voice search, category scoping, trending and recent searches, no-results page with kathputli and suggestions.
Growth and retention: coupons, first-order offer, bundles, festival campaigns, flash sales with countdown, referral program, review-incentive emails, back-in-stock, post-purchase cross-sell, email and WhatsApp flows (welcome, abandoned cart, shipped, delivered, review, win-back), UTM and analytics events (GA4, Meta Pixel), A/B-test hooks.
