• Other: Contact (form, map, WhatsApp, hours), FAQ (accordion, searchable), Shipping and Returns, Privacy, Terms, Size Guide, Care Guide, Track Order, Store Locator (optional), Careers (optional), 404 and 500 with kathputli, offline page.
10. ADMIN PANEL
Products and variants CRUD with image upload, inventory, categories, coupons, banners (editable hero and carousel), orders (status, shipment, refunds), customers, B2B applications and quotes, blog, reviews moderation, analytics dashboard (sales, conversion, AOV, top crafts, abandoned carts), roles and permissions, CSV import and export.
11. ANIMATION AND INTERACTION RULES
• Easing and timing: 250 to 600 ms for UI, up to 1.2 s for hero choreography; consistent ease (cubic-bezier(.22,1,.36,1)).
• Micro-interactions: add-to-cart (item flies to cart icon with a small bounce and jhankar), heart burst, button leheriya fill, input focus glow, toast with kathputli bell.
• Hover: image zoom plus second-image swap, 3D tilt on feature cards, magnetic CTAs.
• Scroll: pinned storytelling, parallax layers, stamp-in borders, counters, progress bar styled as a thread.
• Performance guardrails: animate only transform and opacity, lazy-load heavy Lottie/Three assets, pause off-screen animations, cap particle counts, GPU-safe on low-end Android. Honour prefers-reduced-motion and provide a 'Reduce animations' toggle in the footer.
• Mobile-first: bottom tab bar (Home, Shop, Wishlist, Cart, Account), swipe gestures, thumb-zone CTAs, 44px+ tap targets.
12. COMPLIANCE, TRUST AND SEO
Indian requirements: GST invoices, Consumer Protection (E-commerce) Rules display (seller details, return policy, grievance officer), DPDP-aligned consent and privacy, cookie banner. Authenticity: GI-tag badges only on genuinely GI-tagged crafts (e.g. Thewa), never invent claims. SEO: crawlable category and craft pages, product schema with reviews, OpenGraph images, canonical URLs, Hindi hreflang, blog schema, fast Core Web Vitals.
13. MOCK PRODUCT DATABASE (100+ PRODUCTS, SEEDED VIA BACKEND AT THE END)
Rule: build every feature against a small dev fixture first (about 10 products). Only in the FINAL phase, after checkout, B2B, search, admin and blog all work, build and run a backend seeding pipeline that loads at least 108 mock products (target 108, never fewer than 100) plus all supporting data into PostgreSQL. Nothing in the UI may hard-code products; every page must read from the database through the API.
Seeding pipeline requirements:
• Location: prisma/seed/ with typed data files (products.ts or products.json), generators and an entry point seed.ts. Commands: npm run seed (idempotent upsert by sku/slug, safe to re-run), npm run seed:reset (wipe mock data and reseed, blocked when NODE_ENV=production), npm run seed:verify (prints counts and fails if products < 100), npm run seed:purge-mock (deletes only rows with isMock = true).
• Also expose an admin-only backend route POST /api/admin/seed (admin role, CSRF-protected, disabled in production unless ALLOW_SEED=true) that runs the same pipeline and returns a JSON summary of inserted and updated rows. The admin panel gets a 'Load demo data' button wired to it.
• Every mock row carries isMock: true so it can be removed before launch without touching real data.
• Seed order (respect foreign keys): artisans, categories and sub-categories, products, variants and inventory, product images, B2B price tiers, reviews, blog posts, coupons, banners, demo users, sample orders, wishlist entries. After inserting, rebuild the search index (Meilisearch/Algolia) and revalidate cached pages.
• Output a final report: counts per table, products per category, any validation failures, and the first five product URLs to open.
Product record (every product must be complete):
• name, unique slug, unique sku (pattern RH-<CAT>-<craft>-<number>), category and sub-category, short and long description (60 to 120 words, warm Rajasthani voice, no false claims), craft type, region/origin town, material, care instructions, occasion tags, colour tags, gender/age tag where relevant.
• Pricing: mrp and price in INR (discount 0 to 35%), GST rate, HSN code, weight and dimensions for shipping.
• Variants: sizes (XS to XXL or free size), colours or sets, each with its own stock count (some low-stock, 3 to 5 items out of stock for back-in-stock testing).
• B2B: wholesale price tiers (for example 10+, 25+, 50+, 100+ units at roughly 12%, 22%, 32%, 40% below retail), MOQ, case-pack size, lead time in days, customisable flag.
• Craft passport: technique, artisan id (link to one of 12 seeded artisans with name, village, years of experience, short story), hours of work, GI-tag flag (true only for crafts that really hold one, such as Thewa; otherwise false).
• Media: 3 to 5 images per product. Because real photography does not exist yet, generate on-brand local placeholder images (SVG or WebP written to public/mock/) using each craft's pattern and the Modern Rajputana palette, with descriptive alt text, and keep an images.csv mapping so real photos can be dropped in later without code changes. Never hotlink or copy images from other brands.
• Merchandising flags: isBestseller, isNewArrival, isFeatured, isFestive, isGiftable (spread sensibly, for example 12 bestsellers, 15 new arrivals, 10 featured).
• Ratings: average 3.9 to 4.9, review counts 0 to 180 (skewed), generated reviews (2 to 6 per product, about 350 in total) with names, cities, star ratings, light Hinglish phrasing, some with 'verified purchase'.
• SEO fields: meta title, meta description, alt texts.
